<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:28:44Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Europe sees new protests over rising costs, inequality and public services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f779439fe5d88ab06f1f1c5bc775e9cb89220a5240e819ea27ed1feafec15056</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:28:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T09:41:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-sees-new-protests-over-rising-costs-inequality-and-public-services--a1d144e53fad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-sees-new-protests-over-rising-costs-inequality-and-public-services" /><summary type="html">Sunday marks the third consecutive day of protests across Europe, following large demonstrations on Friday and smaller rallies on Saturday, from Portugal to France. The protests have largely focused on the rising cost of living and access to affordable housing. In France, demonstrations have now taken place for six weekends in a row. Ophelie Jacobson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: Ukrainian rescuers search for survivors in rubble after Russian attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:185963357f0556cc78353eb11c6b97fe965ee6c98657c33a2fcff4f2f4367a95</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T06:15:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261122-live-finland-says-war-spilling-over-after-baltic-sea-drone-strike-on-russian-cargo-ship--98ee191af9fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261122-live-finland-says-war-spilling-over-after-baltic-sea-drone-strike-on-russian-cargo-ship" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian rescue teams on Sunday searched for survivors in the rubble of a collapsed residential building in Dymer, in the Kyiv region, after a Russian drone strike, which killed two people and wounded four others. Meanwhile, Finland warned the war was "spilling over" after a drone set fire to a Russian cargo ship in the Baltic Sea Saturday. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU-Indonesia agreement sees the light after ten years of negotiations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01f3dfe2f8319e496731d380b39278c16b9b3dcbe31ad90e522e4ccc2751195b</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T22:23:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261121-eu-indonesia-agreement-sees-the-light-after-ten-years-of-negotiations--6b9c7be2271c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261121-eu-indonesia-agreement-sees-the-light-after-ten-years-of-negotiations" /><summary type="html">The European Union and Indonesia have signed a major trade deal, ten years after talks began.The agreement removes almost all tariffs between the EU and Southeast Asia's biggest economy: 98.5 per cent of them. For Europe, it means access to a market of 280 million people and a steadier supply of nickel for batteries. For Indonesia, easier exports of palm oil, textiles and footwear, and it arrives just before its current EU trade preferences end on the 1st of January. To discuss the deal Airlangga Hartarto, Coordinating Minister for Economic Affairs in Indonesia joined us on the programme.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia attacks Zelensky's hometown, Ukraine reaffirms wish to join NATO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:000afd0df7e691a35a10a59d8077946f61d2dcf929d51f34e4bfb93888cfc197</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T19:56:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-russia-attacks-zelensky-s-hometown-ukraine-reaffirms-wish-to-join-nato--7bb8a856bfbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-russia-attacks-zelensky-s-hometown-ukraine-reaffirms-wish-to-join-nato" /><summary type="html">A Russian ballistic missile attack on President Volodymyr Zelensky’s hometown in central Ukraine on Saturday killed two people and wounded dozens. Hours later, Zelensky reiterated his country's determination to join NATO, following proposals to provide Kyiv with security guarantees similar to those of the military alliance.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia launches ballistic missile attack on Zelensky's hometown in central Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b553c8eea4ee4ce7105ac3b78297bb2437480aa4351aef084fe3b5f4f5457f48</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T19:55:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-launches-ballistic-missile-attack-on-zelensky-s-hometown-in-central-ukraine--9ccdbee28248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-launches-ballistic-missile-attack-on-zelensky-s-hometown-in-central-ukraine" /><summary type="html">A Russian ballistic missile attack on President Volodymyr Zelensky’s hometown in central Ukraine on Saturday killed two people and wounded dozens. Hours later, Zelensky reiterated his country's determination to join NATO. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>Drone attack sets Russian cargo ship ablaze in Gulf of Finland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5651baa90aea88fed148a6d07e5d0b48b79f090a800309efdc59038b2d0646dd</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T18:02:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland--6ddedb55210c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland" /><summary type="html">A Russian cargo ship caught fire after ​being hit by drones in the Baltic Sea on Saturday and drifted into Finnish waters. Reporting from Kyiv, FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg notes that the ship is affiliated with a major Russian military logistics company. While Ukrainian authorities typically neither confirm nor deny responsibility, analysts cite a clear motive for the targeting, Cragg explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Drone attack sets Russian cargo ship ablaze in Gulf of Finland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe636a668ab0927c0acec44878e95da01dc517799ef459f4fcbe1cdee6e382a3</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T12:35:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland--c7c9c4110e34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland" /><summary type="html">A Russian cargo ship caught fire after a drone strike in international waters in the Gulf of Finland on Saturday and later drifted into the country's ⁠territorial waters, Finnish authorities said. Helsinki alerted NATO and imposed temporary restrictions in the area amid heightened tensions in the Baltic Sea.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Accept cookies'? Russia collects data from swaths of unknowing Swedes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ccfa0a71065bfefaa3c4ec601141f4cccd0cad0262eff877d6eb7efe8ef33ac</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T10:55:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-accept-cookies-russia-collected-data-swaths-unknowing-swedes--a6892ead2cc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-accept-cookies-russia-collected-data-swaths-unknowing-swedes" /><summary type="html">A Russian tech firm backed by an oligarch close to President Vladimir Putin has secretly been collecting data from hundreds of thousands – possibly millions – of Swedes, a newspaper investigation found. The revelation has rattled the Nordic nation, whose proximity to Russia and unusually open public records system make it particularly vulnerable to Moscow’s hybrid war tactics.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Unacceptable': EU chief condemns alleged Russian plot to kill US-Ukrainian citizen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d6319b9128cc2b302e73f886fd077cd67fd1db374e684883e6ca5227c573b5b</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T10:32:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-unacceptable-eu-chief-condemns-alleged-russian-plot-to-kill-us-ukrainian-citizen--dca3e06988cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-unacceptable-eu-chief-condemns-alleged-russian-plot-to-kill-us-ukrainian-citizen" /><summary type="html">European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen condemned an alleged Russian intelligence plot to assassinate a US-Ukrainian citizen in Denmark, vowing full solidarity with Copenhagen.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU, UK reach reset deal after Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8eccfa483ccdc16b582b11ba0d24fdef54807372d3a644cc1b691b3a400f7434</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T09:43:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-uk-reach-reset-deal-after-brexit--3244a7b00c69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-uk-reach-reset-deal-after-brexit" /><summary type="html">The UK and the EU signed three agreements on Friday at a summit in Brussels, marking a new effort to reset post-Brexit relations. The deals aim to reduce red tape for food exports, link emissions trading schemes and allow tens of thousands of young people to live and work more freely across the Channel. Prime Minister Andy Burnham has called Brexit an “obvious failure” to deliver on its promises and wants to deepen ties with the EU, a position criticised by veteran Brexiteer Nigel Farage, who has warned of a political backlash. Daniel Quinlan has this story.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK and EU strike ‘landmark’ deal to rebuild ties after Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12fd8c7cbfea0fe004dbc6d9b013fa696071327b8c9de4319857b78cbf9ed8be</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T17:06:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-uk-and-eu-strike-landmark-deal-to-rebuild-ties-after-brexit--fb622c5a1ee8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-uk-and-eu-strike-landmark-deal-to-rebuild-ties-after-brexit" /><summary type="html">🇬🇧🇪🇺 A fresh start after #Brexit? The #UK and #EU have agreed on a landmark #deal to rebuild ties, following a summit in Brussels this Friday. The agreement covers easier food export checks, youth mobility and carbon emission quotas.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘A more expensive EU is not a better EU’: Austria's Minister for Europe, Claudia Bauer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:823b68de0a0672b459a95020ca6aad9cb1f4a7f4526f645b378feddfb5421f90</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T16:53:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-a-more-expensive-eu-is-not-a-better-eu-austria-s-minister-for-europe-claudia-bauer--aeea629ca19f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-a-more-expensive-eu-is-not-a-better-eu-austria-s-minister-for-europe-claudia-bauer" /><summary type="html">This week's programme hosted Claudia Bauer, Austria’s Federal Minister for Europe, Integration and Family while she was in Paris for the recent G7 meeting. She offered her thoughts on the diplomatic moves surrounding Ukraine, transatlantic relations, EU enlargement and a headscarf ban in Austrian schools that has caused disquiet. We also talked about the thorny negotiations involved in the EU’s next long-term budget: the Multiannual Financial Framework.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spain’s political crossroads, Europe’s wider stakes: Spaniards to vote in key election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b0ecba7cdac86ccf75d0baf500fd210f169be91e42656a72913244dc5cbf925</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:17:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-spains-political-crossroads-europes-wider-stakes-spaniards-to-vote-in-key-election--45b0fdce8813.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-spains-political-crossroads-europes-wider-stakes-spaniards-to-vote-in-key-election" /><summary type="html">The stakes are high – not only for people in Spain, but also for Europe. On November 29, the country holds a parliamentary election that could see the end of the Socialist-led government and potentially a coalition between the right and the far right, in one of the EU’s biggest and most influential member states. It could also signal the end of Pedro Sanchez’s third term in office. Among other things, the prime minister may pay the political price for two shocking train crashes and the migrant crisis in Spain’s North African exclave of Ceuta.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Does staggered consent actually protect young people?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e542159c3ba01dd84f742d0234b654f0fb213f8f84505d4ddc3a1e32b5b99be</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261120-does-staggered-consent-actually-protect-young-people--b74fdbb9cde1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261120-does-staggered-consent-actually-protect-young-people" /><summary type="html">Following recent scandals involving two iconic British comedians, the UK government is considering the introduction of staggered age consent. Annette Young talks to Katherine Allen from the Institute of Social Justice and Crime in the UK about whether such laws work. Also the social costs of femicide; how do loved ones cope with such a loss, and what support is available to families in the wake of such a tragedy? Plus we meet the women who are challenging the traditions of Mexican mariachi music, a world that remains largely male dominated.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Poland slams Russian 'provocation' as missiles land near European military drills</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62b2caa583753c64fd4c039322f9a498092c3c48539b498bf50dba74e3a4dadf</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T10:38:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-poland-says-russian-missile-hit-its-territory-during-attack-on-ukraine--6a169bd9648e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-poland-says-russian-missile-hit-its-territory-during-attack-on-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Two Russian missiles and a suspected drone came down in Poland on Friday in what Prime Minister Donald Tusk said was likely an "intentional provocation" timed to coincide with European military exercises in the country for a possible postwar mission in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Young people across Europe stage mass 'fight for our future' protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d64cfaee10a362ddd211eb60eeb5eb4b5229ae3ad79b17599cfa0de4453ce17</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T07:57:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-europe-s-youth-set-to-join-mass-cost-of-living-protests-in-25-countries--899f9a82f73c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-europe-s-youth-set-to-join-mass-cost-of-living-protests-in-25-countries" /><summary type="html">A fresh wave of student protests took place across Europe Friday, inspired by demonstrations that have rocked France for weeks. Their demands range from more funding for education to climate justice and even ending conscription. Further youth protests are set to take place across the continent over the weekend.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France seeks UN Security Council meeting after Russian strikes hit European embassies in Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5a1120bee16d06d70400d01e4f791959a8b61e86e0febb7716e94fc321eeff0</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T06:32:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-live-deadly-russian-attacks-damage-two-bridges-in-kyiv-mayor-says--388c1dca5fe6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-live-deadly-russian-attacks-damage-two-bridges-in-kyiv-mayor-says" /><summary type="html">France called for a UN Security Council meeting following a salvo of Russian strikes on Ukraine Friday that damaged the Austrian and Dutch embassies in Kyiv, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said. The new wave of missile and drone attacks came after Russian President Vladimir Putin vowed a "painful" response to Ukraine's strike on a bridge that links occupied Crimea with the Russian mainland. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Czechs protest en masse against growing concentration of power, threats to press freedom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d21b47fa8032fedb2474cb516ce31cc3762608cd6dbcea9a2e92cd580c57a57</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T06:02:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-czechs-protest-en-masse-against-concentration-of-power-in-one-hand-and-growing-control-over--9a7dcdecced1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-czechs-protest-en-masse-against-concentration-of-power-in-one-hand-and-growing-control-over-media" /><summary type="html">As large demonstrations in the Czech Republic challenge Prime Minister Andrej Babiš's plans to change the funding model of public broadcasters, Chair of the Million Moments for Democracy movement Mikuláš Minář joins François Picard from Prague for Spotlight, warning that his country risks following Hungary and Slovakia in democratic backsliding. "We are really afraid that the Czech Republic is following the Orbánian Hungarian way, (Fico's) Slovakian way," he says.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Burnham hails 'landmark' EU-UK deal on trade, youth mobility as 'good day' for Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b03d58a12df5ec09b7a9e362452cfcf1f399cca6d4f068a966c4eb625a1b77a</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T02:00:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-eu-and-uk-set-to-sign-deals-on-trade-energy-youth-mobility-at-brussels-summit--38d65333a954.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-eu-and-uk-set-to-sign-deals-on-trade-energy-youth-mobility-at-brussels-summit" /><summary type="html">The United Kingdom and European Union agreed to a new deal on trade, energy and youth mobility on Friday, which UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham called a "good day" for both London and the bloc. Burnham – who has said he hopes to see Britain rejoin the EU in his lifetime – argues the deals will help fix some of the damage Brexit inflicted.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>PM Sanchez admits 'mistakes' in key debate ahead of Spain's election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a87a6debefe6f38e1d061053e8ce829a476a8fab1b7e6127cc77c0f4367dbee</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T00:49:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-pm-s_nchez-admits-mistakes-in-key-debate-ahead-of-spain-election--31911ebf68da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-pm-s%C3%A1nchez-admits-mistakes-in-key-debate-ahead-of-spain-election" /><summary type="html">Spain's Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez acknowledged shortcomings in his government on Thursday as he faced conservative rival Alberto Nunez Feijoo in the campaign's only televised debate. The November 29 election could leave the far-right Vox party in a position to enter government.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian strikes on Kyiv kill one, damage Dutch and Austrian embassies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd831dac198fb91edf141da4a11fb1c14ee3dbb1e5babd816827974d4eda502c</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T21:25:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-strikes-on-kyiv-kill-one-damage-dutch-and-austrian-embassies--b11b79f67545.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-strikes-on-kyiv-kill-one-damage-dutch-and-austrian-embassies" /><summary type="html">A wave of daytime Russian strikes on Kyiv on Thursday killed one person and damaged a historic cathedral as well as the embassies of Austria and the Netherlands. Loud explosions erupted across the Ukraine capital throughout the day as the leaders of Russia, China and the United States held a historic meeting in China that put Russia's President Vladimir Putin in international spotlight. FRANCE 24's Laurent Berstecher reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kushner says Trump 'open' to extend NATO mutual defense-type clause to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:705069c065fbc85ccda774fee487a00aae0d9ab586f995a07bd6764487e0c6a4</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T20:41:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kushner-says-trump-open-to-extend-nato-mutual-defense-type-clause-to-ukraine--5d7323eefe85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kushner-says-trump-open-to-extend-nato-mutual-defense-type-clause-to-ukraine" /><summary type="html">US envoy Jared Kushner said Thursday that President Donald Trump was open to extending to Ukraine a security guarantee similar to NATO's mutual defense clause, but stressed that Washington has to protect its interests too. The comments came as German Chancellor Friedrich Merz qualified the summit between the presidents of the United States, Russia and China as a "photo op". FRANCE 24's international affairs commentator Douglas Herbert explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron urges Ukraine's allies to 'reopen the question' of NATO membership</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9672f7756f82faed7bfafa1125ba1bb3d267a0049a5122155eafccace31bc398</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T20:32:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-macron-urges-ukraine-allies-reopen-question-nato-membership--3461324b88d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-macron-urges-ukraine-allies-reopen-question-nato-membership" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Thursday called for Ukraine's allies to speed up the delivery of urgently needed air defence systems and urged them to "reopen the question" of Ukraine's NATO membership after talks in Berlin aimed at reaffirming European support for Kyiv.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Three of a kind? Xi hosts Trump and Putin as Ukraine war grinds on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e0f4c592b8c8c03c43c6c96fb4e7454c46afaefbe5ca5c3ebd8b2108b82b5b7</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T19:39:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261119-three-of-a-kind-xi-hosts-trump-and-putin-as-ukraine-war-grinds-on--0d31e6ae5346.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261119-three-of-a-kind-xi-hosts-trump-and-putin-as-ukraine-war-grinds-on" /><summary type="html">Gang of three or glorified photo op? Chinese President Xi Jinping is hosting his US and Russian counterparts Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin on the sidelines of the APEC summit. Already, our Monday panel rejected attempts to paint the three-way meeting as a new Yalta, in reference to the 1945 sit-down on the Black Sea that defined the post-war security architecture of Europe.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Behind the UK's use of AI in asylum applications</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea094185d2392ecc05093db21207e68dc209ac868dcf9c48b7ff5a416a790b53</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:07:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/behind-the-uk-s-use-of-ai-in-asylum-applications--7c816cd4e664.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/behind-the-uk-s-use-of-ai-in-asylum-applications" /><summary type="html">The UK is increasingly turning to artificial intelligence to manage its immigration system, from analysing migrants’ phones to processing asylum applications. But what happens when AI gets involved in deciding how an asylum seeker's story is understood? Stella Elgersma, journalist at InfoMigrants, explains how the UK Home Office is testing AI tools to process asylum applications, including a system that generates summaries of asylum interviews. With errors, limited human oversight and concerns over transparency, could AI put asylum seekers’ lives at risk?</summary></entry><entry><title>China summit ends with little new, Europe backs Ukraine in Berlin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bcbafc4026d7aa3585d103ee0a9c18e572c4457ff05509535383ba5d1c96c02</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T14:04:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/china-summit-ends-with-little-new-europe-backs-ukraine-in-berlin--41fb764541d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/china-summit-ends-with-little-new-europe-backs-ukraine-in-berlin" /><summary type="html">The leaders of China, the United States and Russia met in Shenzhen for a historic first, but the summit brought little new: non-binding statements on peace and no plan to meet regularly. In Berlin, Europeans gathered to show their support for Ukraine, a pointed answer to a summit where Europe had no seat, as FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's European allies meet in Berlin in show of support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:846c3edceaed67999ba3d790c8fface0990f79e485f995e42504dc708afc7b5e</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T10:43:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-s-european-allies-meet-in-berlin-in-show-of-support--2eee6bb2adfc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-s-european-allies-meet-in-berlin-in-show-of-support" /><summary type="html">Ukraine’s main European allies are meeting in Berlin on Thursday as a show of support for Kyiv, with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner also attending. The gathering, which brings together the leaders of Germany, France, Britain, Poland and Italy as well as NATO chief Mark Rutte, takes place as Trump and Putin meet in China, fuelling fears in Europe that decisions on the war could be made without its input. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Germany has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Denmark ratifies Greenland security deal after months of pressure by Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6a8a63d1d63c33b4a51fdc3f015c6db168babd362398fa37914f98fbd6c0616</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T10:08:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-denmark-ratifies-greenland-security-deal-after-months-of-pressure-by-trump--274d8e9dcbf1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-denmark-ratifies-greenland-security-deal-after-months-of-pressure-by-trump" /><summary type="html">Denmark's parliament on Thursday ratified a security deal involving Greenland and the United States. The vote comes months after the US, Denmark and Greenland ​signed the ‌agreement to end a standoff with the Trump administration over the Arctic island's future.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's allies meet in Berlin to rally support for Kyiv after Trump-Putin-Xi talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95175e0ed9ad34ceed00901547ebfb62f5ddea8c16c607fde98c55abd58b86e4</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T02:55:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-european-leaders-to-meet-in-berlin-to-support-for-ukraine-after-trump-putin-xi-talks--3d07d30f658f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-european-leaders-to-meet-in-berlin-to-support-for-ukraine-after-trump-putin-xi-talks" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's allies meet in Berlin on Thursday to shore up support for Kyiv just hours after Russia's Vladimir Putin took part in a historic trilateral meeting with US President Donald Trump and China's Xi Jinping. The "Coalition of the Willing" summit comes as Europe is hoping to secure a seat at the table of any future peace talks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: Vanuatu calls for UN climate summit reform, warns of backsliding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:724b81326c02dddfed36006cd14395beb6fb59dfe722e938d91a53300e96e91f</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T02:00:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-cop31-vanuatu-un-climate-summit-reform-warns-of-backsliding--3de44bf4c890.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-cop31-vanuatu-un-climate-summit-reform-warns-of-backsliding" /><summary type="html">Vanuatu's Environment Minister Ralph Regenvanu has called for changes to the UN climate summit process, accusing a small group of countries of blocking progress and warning that COP31 risks reversing previous commitments.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
